1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:07,184
This is Capy Care: a calm crew of AI agents
that does one real job for families.

2
00:00:07,184 --> 00:00:11,014
It keeps an aging parent's
medications straight.

3
00:00:11,864 --> 00:00:17,378
When Mom comes home from the hospital, her
discharge papers say lisinopril, 5 mg.

4
00:00:17,378 --> 00:00:21,463
Three days later, the new bottle from
the pharmacy says ten.

5
00:00:21,463 --> 00:00:22,756
Which one is right?

6
00:00:22,756 --> 00:00:23,641
In one study,

7
00:00:23,641 --> 00:00:29,836
two out of three patients left the hospital with a
discrepancy in their medication records.

8
00:00:30,686 --> 00:00:33,138
So we built a team of four capybaras.

9
00:00:33,138 --> 00:00:36,452
Capy Reader reads everything
with Superlinked SIE.

10
00:00:36,452 --> 00:00:40,760
Elder Capy remembers every fact, and
when it happened, in Cognee.

11
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:44,803
Capy Pharmacist checks the official
drug label with Keenable.

12
00:00:44,803 --> 00:00:49,442
And Capy Guardian keeps the family in the
loop, in a shared Band room.

13
00:00:50,292 --> 00:00:52,120
Here it is, running live.

14
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:56,871
Lily shares Mom's discharge papers and
a photo of the new bottle.

15
00:00:56,871 --> 00:01:03,011
SIE reads each one in about a second: docling for
the PDF, LightOnOCR for the photo,

16
00:01:03,011 --> 00:01:07,471
and GLiNER2 pulls out every
medication and dose, with no LLM.

17
00:01:07,471 --> 00:01:10,687
Elder Capy stores each source with its date,

18
00:01:10,687 --> 00:01:14,854
and Cognee's conflict review
catches it: 5 mg versus ten.

19
00:01:14,854 --> 00:01:19,240
The Pharmacist reads the real label,
live, through Keenable.

20
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:20,848
Both doses are normal,

21
00:01:20,848 --> 00:01:25,819
so the Guardian asks Lily to call the
pharmacy before the next dose.

22
00:01:26,669 --> 00:01:28,698
Lily calls, and replies: Dr.

23
00:01:28,698 --> 00:01:31,526
Alvarez raised the dose on November 10.

24
00:01:31,526 --> 00:01:36,383
GLiNER2 reads her answer, and Cognee
records the family's decision,

25
00:01:36,383 --> 00:01:38,920
so it holds on every future review.

26
00:01:41,270 --> 00:01:46,406
Then her brother Sam sends a voice note:
Mom's been dizzy since Wednesday.

27
00:01:46,406 --> 00:01:49,460
Whisper on SIE transcribes it in one second.

28
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:55,151
Elder Capy asks Cognee a question about time:
what changed right before Wednesday?

29
00:01:55,151 --> 00:01:57,372
The dose went up the day before.

30
00:01:57,372 --> 00:02:03,202
The official label lists dizziness as a common
side effect, so Qwen, running on SIE,

31
00:02:03,202 --> 00:02:07,366
writes a one-page brief with three
questions for the doctor.

32
00:02:08,216 --> 00:02:11,641
Under the hood, SIE senses and
Cognee remembers.

33
00:02:11,641 --> 00:02:16,706
Even Cognee's own language model and
embeddings run on Superlinked SIE.

34
00:02:17,556 --> 00:02:19,846
Capy Care flags, and never advises.

35
00:02:19,846 --> 00:02:25,210
A person makes every call, and the family walks
into the doctor's office prepared.
